In this project, I implemented a Diamond Star Pattern program using C++.
* Used nested loops to create the diamond shape.
* Printed the upper half of the diamond pattern.
* Printed the lower half of the diamond pattern.
* Managed spaces and stars to maintain proper alignment.
* Applied mathematical logic to control the number of stars in each row.
* Practiced nested loops and pattern generation techniques.
* Improved understanding of symmetry and structured output design.
* Tested the program to ensure the diamond pattern was displayed correctly.
This project helped me strengthen my understanding of loops, nested loops, pattern printing, and logical problem-solving in C++.
